 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T12:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**Probably yes, if you’re generally healthy—but keep it easy.** Around **12:40–12:45 pm in Penang on October 17**, readings ranged from **US AQI 53–101**: George Town was **93 (moderate)**, while Bukit Mertajam was **101 (unhealthy for sensitive groups)**. Check the reading for your exact area before heading out, since it varies across Penang. ([iqair.com](https://www.iqair.com/air-quality/malaysia/penang))\n\nIf you have asthma or heart or lung disease, or you’re unusually sensitive to pollution, choose a shorter, gentler run or exercise indoors—especially if your local reading is over 100. It’s also about **31°C (88°F)** in George Town, so the heat may be a bigger reason to wait until it cools down. ([document.airnow.gov](https://document.airnow.gov/technical-assistance-document-for-the-reporting-of-daily-air-quailty.pdf?utm_source=openai))",
